{{also|pull out}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From the verb phrase {{m|en|pull out}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[withdrawal]], especially of [[armed forces]].
# The [[change]] of the [[flight]] of an [[aircraft]] from a [[dive]] to [[level]] flight.
# An object, such as a [[newspaper]] [[supplement]], that can be [[pulled]] [[out]] from something else.
# {{lb|en|typography}} {{synonym of|liftout|lang=en||quotation given special visual treatment}}
# An [[area]] by the side of a road where [[vehicle]]s may [[temporarily]] stop in safety.  Typical pullouts allow [[driver]]s and [[passenger]]s to safely exit the vehicle but rarely have additional [[amenities]].
#* {{quote-web|first=Paul|last=Elias|first2=Phoung|last2=Le|Title=CHP: Deadly SUV Cliff Crash May Have Been Intentional|url=https://www.usnews.com/news/best-states/california/articles/2018-04-01/chp-deadly-suv-cliff-crash-may-have-been-intentional|accessdate=2018-04-05|work=www.usnews.com|publisher=Associated Press;U.S. News and World Report|date=2018-04-01|passage=Capt. Greg Baarts with the CHP Northern Division says information pulled from the SUV's software shows the vehicle was stopped at the highway '''pullout''' before it accelerated straight off the cliff.}}

